WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.970
Right now, each of your cells is
running thousands of reactions at once.

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.770
Many are linked into pathways: chains
where the product of one step becomes the

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.150
starting material for the next.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.320
Yet a cell can slow down one pathway, and
leave the rest of its metabolism running.

5
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:22.220
So how can a single molecule switch
off one reaction among thousands?

6
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.810
In this mission, you'll read data on
two mystery molecules that both slow the

7
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.370
same reaction.

8
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.750
Then you'll work out
how to tell them apart,

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.680
from the numbers alone.

10
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:37.510
Your mission: find out how a single
molecule can switch off one reaction among

11
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.530
thousands.
